{"duration": 54.952, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "Thomas Edison slammed a tiny carbon button into his telegraph.", "start": 0.08, "end": 3.508}, {"beat": 0, "text": "He hoped the speck could carry a voice across town.", "start": 3.728, "end": 6.047}, {"beat": 1, "text": "His lab mates scoffed, insisting the steel diaphragm was sufficient.", "start": 6.467, "end": 10.099}, {"beat": 1, "text": "They warned him he\u2019d waste time on a useless gimmick.", "start": 10.319, "end": 12.75}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Early telephone calls were faint, often disappearing mid\u2011sentence.", "start": 13.17, "end": 16.712}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Customers complained they could barely hear each other.", "start": 16.932, "end": 19.45}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Edison tightened the button, pressed the granules harder, and tried again.", "start": 19.67, "end": 23.2}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Each tweak made the signal a little louder.", "start": 23.42, "end": 25.283}, {"beat": 3, "text": "You see, it\u2019s like whispering into a tin can.", "start": 25.703, "end": 27.943}, {"beat": 3, "text": "Versus shouting through a megaphone.", "start": 28.163, "end": 29.93}, {"beat": 4, "text": "When sound hits the thin diaphragm, it squeezes carbon granules.", "start": 30.35, "end": 33.953}, {"beat": 4, "text": "The pressure lowers the granules\u2019 electrical resistance.", "start": 34.173, "end": 37.007}, {"beat": 4, "text": "A steady current then varies, creating a strong electric pulse.", "start": 37.227, "end": 40.524}, {"beat": 4, "text": "That pulse travels the whole line without extra batteries.", "start": 40.744, "end": 43.793}, {"beat": 5, "text": "That tiny button let phones ring miles on a single wire.", "start": 44.213, "end": 47.09}, {"beat": 5, "text": "It became the standard for a whole century of telephony.", "start": 47.31, "end": 50.003}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Even after vacuum tubes arrived, the carbon transmitter still ruled.", "start": 50.223, "end": 53.83